# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# mutation testing — Stryker's sandbox holds full copies of the source tree with
# `// @ts-nocheck` injected at the top of every file. Untracked AND unlinted:
# see the ignores in eslint.config.mjs and the exclude in tsconfig.json, because
# .husky/pre-push runs a full-repo `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck` that would
# otherwise fail for everyone who has ever run the mutation suite.
/.stryker-tmp/
/reports/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files — .env.example is the only committed env file
.env*
!.env.example

# real staff data (Kenya DPA) — only scripts/staff.example.csv (synthetic)
# may ever be committed
seed-data/

# real client exports (Kenya DPA). The legacy export carries staff names,
# serials, PO numbers and cost centres — it is the client's live asset data and
# must never enter git history, where it cannot be un-committed. Unlike
# seed-data/ these land in docs/, a committed directory, so a stray
# `git add docs/` would take them.
#
# REPO-WIDE BY EXTENSION, NOT BY DIRECTORY, and that distinction is the whole
# point. The first version of this rule was `docs/*.xlsx` — a pattern containing
# a slash, which git anchors to this file's directory, so it matched
# docs/export.xlsx and NOT docs/features/AM-04/export.xlsx. AM-04 creates
# docs/features/AM-04/, and parking a copy of the export beside its design doc
# is exactly the plausible mistake. A depth-enumerated glob that reads as
# repo-wide is the failure class; verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
#
# The negation keeps the synthetic examples committable — they are the fixtures
# the real files must never become (same rule as scripts/staff.example.csv).
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
!*.example.csv

# vercel
.vercel

# local agent configuration and memory — machine-specific notes about this
# developer's setup, never repo content
.claude/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.pnpm-store
